IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III, sections 23 to 23B -- layer 1: what a court that convicts a person of a terrorist-property offence,
-- or of a terrorism offence, may order forfeited; the owner's right to be heard; the Scottish procedure.
-- Every forfeiture rule is a power ("may order"), so a case outside it is NOTHING and never JUST FALSE: the Act does not say the court
-- may not forfeit the property some other way (reading M2).  "Ancillary offence" and "terrorist connection" turn on the Counter-Terrorism
-- Act 2008, Schedule 4 on a Schedule not among the sources: facts the caller states.  Section 23A(5) (the power to amend the list by
-- order) is machinery: inert, reason 2.

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Forfeiture`

§§ `s 23 Forfeiture: terrorist property offences`

-- src:554 | (1) The court by or before which a person is convicted of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 may make a forfeiture order in accordance with the provisions of this section.
@ref s 23(1) (src:554)
GIVEN `the person is convicted by or before the court of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(1) the court may make a forfeiture order` IS
    BRANCH
        -- fork F7: "any of sections 15 to 18" includes section 17A, which lies inside the range
        IF `the person is convicted by or before the court of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court by or before which a person is convicted of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 may make a forfeiture order in accordance with the provisions of this section." (a court that did not convict is not said to lack the power)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:555 | (2) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 15(1) or (2) or 16, the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which—
-- src:556 | (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or
-- src:557 | (b) they intended should be used, or had reasonable cause to suspect might be used, for those purposes.
@ref s 23(2) (src:555-557)
GIVEN `the offence of which the person is convicted` IS A `Offence of Part III`
      `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(2) the court may order the forfeiture of the property` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence of which the person is convicted`
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(1)` THEN `s 23(2) the property is within the subsection` `the property`
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(2)` THEN `s 23(2) the property is within the subsection` `the property`
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(1)` THEN `s 23(2) the property is within the subsection` `the property`
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(2)` THEN `s 23(2) the property is within the subsection` `the property`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 15(1) or (2) or 16" (a "where" condition that is not met: the person was convicted of a different offence; ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17A` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 18` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:555 | (2) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 15(1) or (2) or 16, the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which—
-- src:556 | (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or
-- src:557 | (b) they intended should be used, or had reasonable cause to suspect might be used, for those purposes.
@ref s 23(2) (src:555-557)
GIVEN `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(2) the property is within the subsection` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property`'s `at the time of the offence the person had it in their possession or under their control`
           AND (`the property`'s `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism`
                OR `the property`'s `the person intended that it should be used for the purposes of terrorism`
                OR `the property`'s `the person had reasonable cause to suspect that it might be used for the purposes of terrorism`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which— (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or (b) they intended should be used, or had reasonable cause to suspect might be used"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:558 | (3) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 15(3) the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which—
-- src:559 | (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or
-- src:560 | (b) which, at that time, they knew or had reasonable cause to suspect would or might be used for those purposes.
@ref s 23(3) (src:558-560)
GIVEN `the offence of which the person is convicted` IS A `Offence of Part III`
      `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(3) the court may order the forfeiture of the property` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence of which the person is convicted`
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(3)` THEN
        IF `the property`'s `at the time of the offence the person had it in their possession or under their control`
           AND (`the property`'s `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism`
                OR `the property`'s `the person knew or had reasonable cause to suspect that it would or might be used for the purposes of terrorism`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which— (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or (b) ... they knew or had reasonable cause to suspect would or might be used"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 15(3)" (a "where" condition that is not met: the person was convicted of a different offence; ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17A` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 18` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:561 | (4) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 17 or 18 the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which—
-- src:562 | (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or
-- src:563 | (b) was, at that time, intended by them to be used for those purposes.
@ref s 23(4) (src:561-563)
GIVEN `the offence of which the person is convicted` IS A `Offence of Part III`
      `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(4) the court may order the forfeiture of the property` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence of which the person is convicted`
    WHEN `an offence under s 17` THEN
        IF `the property`'s `at the time of the offence the person had it in their possession or under their control`
           AND (`the property`'s `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism` OR `the property`'s `the person intended that it should be used for the purposes of terrorism`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which— (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or (b) was, at that time, intended by them to be used for those purposes"
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `an offence under s 18` THEN
        IF `the property`'s `at the time of the offence the person had it in their possession or under their control`
           AND (`the property`'s `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism` OR `the property`'s `the person intended that it should be used for the purposes of terrorism`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which, at the time of the offence, the person had in their possession or under their control and which— (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or (b) was, at that time, intended by them to be used for those purposes"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 17 or 18" (a "where" condition that is not met: the person was convicted of a different offence; ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17A` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:564 | (5) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 17 the court may order the forfeiture of the money or other property to which the arrangement in question related, and which—
-- src:565 | (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or
-- src:566 | (b) at the time of the offence, the person knew or had reasonable cause to suspect would or might be used for those purposes.
@ref s 23(5) (src:564-566)
GIVEN `the offence of which the person is convicted` IS A `Offence of Part III`
      `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(5) the court may order the forfeiture of the property` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence of which the person is convicted`
    WHEN `an offence under s 17` THEN
        IF `the property`'s `the arrangement in question related to it`
           AND (`the property`'s `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism`
                OR `the property`'s `the person knew or had reasonable cause to suspect that it would or might be used for the purposes of terrorism`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of the money or other property to which the arrangement in question related, and which— (a) had been used for the purposes of terrorism, or (b) at the time of the offence, the person knew or had reasonable cause to suspect would or might be used"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 17" (a "where" condition that is not met: the person was convicted of a different offence; ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17A` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 18` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:567 | (5A) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 17A the court may order the forfeiture of the amount paid under, or purportedly under, the insurance contract.
@ref s 23(5A) (src:567)
GIVEN `the offence of which the person is convicted` IS A `Offence of Part III`
      `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(5A) the court may order the forfeiture of the amount` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence of which the person is convicted`
    WHEN `an offence under s 17A` THEN
        IF `the property`'s `it is the amount paid under, or purportedly under, the insurance contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of the amount paid under, or purportedly under, the insurance contract"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 17A" (a "where" condition that is not met: the person was convicted of a different offence; ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 18` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:568 | (6) Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 18 the court may order the forfeiture of the money or other property to which the arrangement in question related.
@ref s 23(6) (src:568)
GIVEN `the offence of which the person is convicted` IS A `Offence of Part III`
      `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(6) the court may order the forfeiture of the property` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence of which the person is convicted`
    WHEN `an offence under s 18` THEN
        IF `the property`'s `the arrangement in question related to it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of the money or other property to which the arrangement in question related"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under section 18" (a "where" condition that is not met: the person was convicted of a different offence; ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(3)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 16(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under s 17A` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:569 | (7) Where a person is convicted of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18, the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which wholly or partly, and directly or indirectly, is received by any person as a payment or other reward in connection with the commission of the offence.
@ref s 23(7) (src:569)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property` IS A `Forfeitable property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(7) the court may order the forfeiture of the payment or reward` IS
    BRANCH
        -- fork F7: "any of sections 15 to 18" includes section 17A
        IF `the person is convicted of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18`
           AND `the property`'s `it was received by any person as a payment or other reward in connection with the commission of the offence`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the forfeiture of any money or other property which wholly or partly, and directly or indirectly, is received by any person as a payment or other reward in connection with the commission of the offence"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 23A Forfeiture: other terrorism offences and offences with a terrorist connection`

-- src:577 | (2) This section applies to an offence under—
-- src:578 | (a) any of the following provisions of this Act—
-- src:579 | section 54 (weapons training);
-- src:580 | section 57, 58 or 58A (possessing things and collecting information for the purposes of terrorism);
-- src:581 | section 58B (entering or remaining in a designated area);
-- src:582 | section 59, 60 or 61 (inciting terrorism outside the United Kingdom);
-- src:583 | (b) any of the following provisions of Part 1 of the Terrorism Act 2006 (c. 11)—
-- src:584 | section 2 (dissemination of terrorist publications);
-- src:585 | section 5 (preparation of terrorist acts);
-- src:586 | section 6 (training for terrorism);
-- src:587 | sections 9 to 11 (offences involving radioactive devices or materials).
@ref s 23A(2) (src:577-587)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence listed in s 23A(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23A(2) this section applies to the offence` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 54 (weapons training)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 57 (possessing things for the purposes of terrorism)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 58 (collecting information for the purposes of terrorism)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 58A (collecting information for the purposes of terrorism)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 58B (entering or remaining in a designated area)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 59 (inciting terrorism outside the United Kingdom)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 60 (inciting terrorism outside the United Kingdom)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2000 section 61 (inciting terrorism outside the United Kingdom)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2006 section 2 (dissemination of terrorist publications)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2006 section 5 (preparation of terrorist acts)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2006 section 6 (training for terrorism)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2006 section 9 (offences involving radioactive devices or materials)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2006 section 10 (offences involving radioactive devices or materials)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Terrorism Act 2006 section 11 (offences involving radioactive devices or materials)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to an offence under— (a) any of the following provisions of this Act ... (b) any of the following provisions of Part 1 of the Terrorism Act 2006" (subsections (3) and (4) extend the section to other offences)
    WHEN `none of these` THEN NOTHING

-- src:588 | (3) This section applies to any ancillary offence (as defined in section 94 of the Counter-Terrorism Act 2008) in relation to an offence listed in subsection (2).
@ref s 23A(3) (src:588)
GIVEN `the offence is an ancillary offence (as defined in section 94 of the Counter-Terrorism Act 2008)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in relation to an offence listed in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23A(3) this section applies to the ancillary offence` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offence is an ancillary offence (as defined in section 94 of the Counter-Terrorism Act 2008)` AND `it is in relation to an offence listed in subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to any ancillary offence (as defined in section 94 of the Counter-Terrorism Act 2008) in relation to an offence listed in subsection (2)." (other offences are dealt with by subsections (2) and (4))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:589 | (4) This section also applies to an offence ... as to which—
-- src:590 | (a) in England and Wales, the court dealing with the offence has determined, in accordance with section 30 of the Counter-Terrorism Act 2008 or section 69 of the Sentencing Code, that the offence has a terrorist connection;
-- src:591 | (b) in Scotland, it has been proved, in accordance with section 31 of that Act, that the offence has a terrorist connection.
@ref s 23A(4) (src:589-591)
GIVEN `in England and Wales, the court dealing with the offence has determined that the offence has a terrorist connection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in Scotland, it has been proved that the offence has a terrorist connection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23A(4) this section applies to the offence with a terrorist connection` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `in England and Wales, the court dealing with the offence has determined that the offence has a terrorist connection` OR `in Scotland, it has been proved that the offence has a terrorist connection` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section also applies to an offence ... as to which— (a) in England and Wales, the court dealing with the offence has determined ... (b) in Scotland, it has been proved" (the subsection is silent on Northern Ireland)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:571 | (1) The court by or before which a person is convicted of an offence to which this section applies may order the forfeiture of any money or other property in relation to which the following conditions are met—
-- src:572 | (a) that it was, at the time of the offence, in the possession or control of the person convicted; and
-- src:573 | (b) that—
-- src:574 | (i) it had been used for the purposes of terrorism,
-- src:575 | (ii) it was intended by that person that it should be used for the purposes of terrorism, or
-- src:576 | (iii) the court believes that it will be used for the purposes of terrorism unless forfeited.
@ref s 23A(1) (src:571-576)
GIVEN `this section applies to the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property` IS A `Terrorism forfeiture facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23A(1) the court may order the forfeiture of the property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `this section applies to the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the property`'s `it was, at the time of the offence, in the possession or control of the person convicted`
           AND (`the property`'s `it had been used for the purposes of terrorism`
                OR `the property`'s `it was intended by that person that it should be used for the purposes of terrorism`
                OR `the property`'s `the court believes that it will be used for the purposes of terrorism unless forfeited`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court by or before which a person is convicted of an offence to which this section applies may order the forfeiture of any money or other property in relation to which the following conditions are met" (property outside the conditions is not said to be immune from forfeiture)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:593 | (6) An order adding an offence to subsection (2) applies only in relation to offences committed after the order comes into force.
@ref s 23A(6) (src:593)
GIVEN `the offence was committed after the order adding it to subsection (2) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23A(6) the order adding the offence to subsection (2) applies to the offence` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offence was committed after the order adding it to subsection (2) came into force` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order adding an offence to subsection (2) applies only in relation to offences committed after the order comes into force."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 23B Forfeiture: supplementary provisions`

-- src:595 | (1) Before making an order under section 23 or 23A, a court must give an opportunity to be heard to any person, other than the convicted person, who claims to be the owner or otherwise interested in anything which can be forfeited under that section.
@ref s 23B(1) (src:595)
GIVEN `the court is about to make an order under s 23 or 23A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the convicted person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claims to be the owner or otherwise interested in anything which can be forfeited under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23B(1) the court must give the person an opportunity to be heard` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to any person, other than the convicted person, who claims to be the owner or otherwise interested"
        IF `the person is the convicted person` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the court is about to make an order under s 23 or 23A` AND `the person claims to be the owner or otherwise interested in anything which can be forfeited under that section`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before making an order under section 23 or 23A, a court must give an opportunity to be heard to any person ... who claims to be the owner or otherwise interested" (a person who makes no claim is not said to have the right)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:595 | (1) Before making an order under section 23 or 23A, a court must give an opportunity to be heard to any person, other than the convicted person, who claims to be the owner or otherwise interested in anything which can be forfeited under that section.
@ref s 23B(1) (src:595)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 23B(1) the court must give an opportunity to be heard` IS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `give an opportunity to be heard`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 23B(1): the court made an order under s 23 or 23A without giving an opportunity to be heard to a person, other than the convicted person, who claims to be the owner of or otherwise interested in the property"

-- src:596 | (2) In considering whether to make an order under section 23 or 23A in respect of any property, a court shall have regard to—
-- src:597 | (a) the value of the property, and
-- src:598 | (b) the likely financial and other effects on the convicted person of the making of the order (taken together with any other order that the court contemplates making).
@ref s 23B(2) (src:596-598)
GIVEN `the court is considering whether to make an order under s 23 or 23A in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23B(2) the court shall have regard to the value of the property and the effects on the convicted person` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court is considering whether to make an order under s 23 or 23A in respect of the property` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In considering whether to make an order under section 23 or 23A in respect of any property, a court shall have regard to—"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:596 | (2) In considering whether to make an order under section 23 or 23A in respect of any property, a court shall have regard to—
-- src:597 | (a) the value of the property, and
-- src:598 | (b) the likely financial and other effects on the convicted person of the making of the order (taken together with any other order that the court contemplates making).
@ref s 23B(2) (src:596-598)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 23B(2) the court must have regard to the value and effects` IS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `have regard to the value of the property and the likely effects of the order on the convicted person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 23B(2): the court did not have regard to the value of the property and the likely financial and other effects on the convicted person of the making of the order"

-- src:599 | (3) A court in Scotland must not make an order under section 23 or 23A except on the application of the prosecutor—
-- src:600 | (a) in proceedings on indictment, when the prosecutor moves for sentence, and
-- src:601 | (b) in summary proceedings, before the court sentences the accused;
-- src:602 | and for the purposes of any appeal or review, an order under either of those sections made by a court in Scotland is a sentence.
@ref s 23B(3) (src:599-602)
GIVEN `the court is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are on indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor applies when moving for sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are summary proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor applies before the court sentences the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23B(3) the court in Scotland is barred from making the order` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the court is in Scotland`)
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court in Scotland must not make an order under section 23 or 23A except on the application of the prosecutor" (courts elsewhere are outside the subsection)
            THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except on the application of the prosecutor— (a) in proceedings on indictment, when the prosecutor moves for sentence, and (b) in summary proceedings, before the court sentences the accused"
        IF (`the proceedings are on indictment` AND `the prosecutor applies when moving for sentence`)
           OR (`the proceedings are summary proceedings` AND `the prosecutor applies before the court sentences the accused`)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:599 | (3) A court in Scotland must not make an order under section 23 or 23A except on the application of the prosecutor—
-- src:600 | (a) in proceedings on indictment, when the prosecutor moves for sentence, and
-- src:601 | (b) in summary proceedings, before the court sentences the accused;
-- src:602 | and for the purposes of any appeal or review, an order under either of those sections made by a court in Scotland is a sentence.
@ref s 23B(3) (src:599-602)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 23B(3) the court in Scotland shall not make the order except on the prosecutor's application` IS
    PARTY `the court`
    SHANT `make a forfeiture order in Scotland other than on the application of the prosecutor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 23B(3): a court in Scotland made an order under s 23 or 23A other than on the application of the prosecutor at the time the subsection requires"

-- src:599 | (3) A court in Scotland must not make an order under section 23 or 23A except on the application of the prosecutor—
-- src:600 | (a) in proceedings on indictment, when the prosecutor moves for sentence, and
-- src:601 | (b) in summary proceedings, before the court sentences the accused;
-- src:602 | and for the purposes of any appeal or review, an order under either of those sections made by a court in Scotland is a sentence.
@ref s 23B(3) sentence (src:599-602)
GIVEN `the order was made by a court in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23B(3) the order of a Scottish court is a sentence for the purposes of any appeal or review` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order was made by a court in Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of any appeal or review, an order under either of those sections made by a court in Scotland is a sentence" (an order made elsewhere is outside the clause)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:603 | (4) Schedule 4 makes further provision in relation to forfeiture orders under section 23 or 23A.
@ref s 23B(4) (src:603)
GIVEN `the order is a forfeiture order under s 23 or 23A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23B(4) Schedule 4 makes further provision for the order` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order is a forfeiture order under s 23 or 23A` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Schedule 4 makes further provision in relation to forfeiture orders under section 23 or 23A", and Schedule 4 is not among the sources, so what it provides is not answered
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
